WEBVTT

00:00:00.372 --> 00:00:01.328
Call teams juggle

00:00:01.328 --> 00:00:02.118
a dialer,

00:00:02.118 --> 00:00:02.941
a chat app,

00:00:02.941 --> 00:00:04.869
spreadsheets and a CRM.

00:00:04.869 --> 00:00:06.079
Meet Conexus,

00:00:06.079 --> 00:00:06.987
the CRM built

00:00:06.987 --> 00:00:08.429
for call teams.

00:00:08.429 --> 00:00:09.827
Here's everything it does,

00:00:09.827 --> 00:00:11.488
and what's coming next.

00:00:12.217 --> 00:00:13.843
Izuku calls Eijiro straight

00:00:13.843 --> 00:00:14.846
from the browser,

00:00:14.846 --> 00:00:15.781
in one click.

00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:17.002
Calls are encrypted

00:00:17.002 --> 00:00:18.991
and recorded automatically.

00:00:18.991 --> 00:00:20.025
Inbound calls ring

00:00:20.025 --> 00:00:20.907
in through your

00:00:20.907 --> 00:00:21.973
IVR and queues.

00:00:21.973 --> 00:00:22.923
After hours,

00:00:22.923 --> 00:00:23.814
callers go straight

00:00:23.814 --> 00:00:24.807
to voicemail.

00:00:24.807 --> 00:00:26.020
Transfer the call with

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:26.845
a note for the

00:00:26.845 --> 00:00:27.577
next agent.

00:00:27.577 --> 00:00:28.862
Shoto reads it before

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.397
he even answers.

00:00:30.771 --> 00:00:32.012
It's 9:42 PM

00:00:32.012 --> 00:00:33.596
in Chicago,

00:00:33.596 --> 00:00:34.492
and Izuku tries

00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:35.574
to call Eijiro.

00:00:35.574 --> 00:00:36.496
With the dialer,

00:00:36.496 --> 00:00:37.919
the server blocks it.

00:00:37.919 --> 00:00:38.894
Calls go out

00:00:38.894 --> 00:00:39.667
from 8 AM

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:40.420
to 9 PM,

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:41.368
their time.

00:00:41.368 --> 00:00:42.560
Each customer gets

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.693
three attempts in

00:00:43.693 --> 00:00:44.710
any 24 hours.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:45.694
And blocked numbers

00:00:45.694 --> 00:00:46.957
are never dialed.

00:00:46.957 --> 00:00:48.001
It's built to keep

00:00:48.001 --> 00:00:49.359
your whole floor inside

00:00:49.359 --> 00:00:51.000
calling-hours rules.

00:00:51.371 --> 00:00:52.512
Your team chat lives

00:00:52.512 --> 00:00:54.029
right inside Conexus,

00:00:54.029 --> 00:00:54.966
with channels,

00:00:54.966 --> 00:00:56.546
DMs and mentions.

00:00:56.546 --> 00:00:57.701
Pin the announcement

00:00:57.701 --> 00:00:58.522
everyone needs,

00:00:58.522 --> 00:00:59.267
and react to

00:00:59.267 --> 00:00:59.960
a big close

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:01.075
in one click.

00:01:01.075 --> 00:01:02.692
With the dialer add-on,

00:01:02.692 --> 00:01:03.589
agents can message

00:01:03.589 --> 00:01:04.442
the floor without

00:01:04.442 --> 00:01:05.470
leaving the call.

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:06.301
The floor lead

00:01:06.301 --> 00:01:07.131
sends the play,

00:01:07.131 --> 00:01:08.063
and the customer

00:01:08.063 --> 00:01:09.317
never waits.

00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:10.215
Set up a

00:01:10.215 --> 00:01:10.822
spiff once,

00:01:10.822 --> 00:01:11.987
and Conexus does the

00:01:11.987 --> 00:01:13.074
counting for you.

00:01:13.074 --> 00:01:14.294
The moment Tanjiro

00:01:14.294 --> 00:01:15.216
closes a sale,

00:01:15.216 --> 00:01:16.198
his balance is

00:01:16.198 --> 00:01:17.976
credited automatically.

00:01:17.976 --> 00:01:19.492
The leaderboard updates live,

00:01:19.492 --> 00:01:20.519
so the whole floor

00:01:20.519 --> 00:01:21.844
sees who's winning.

00:01:21.844 --> 00:01:22.755
Every dollar lands

00:01:22.755 --> 00:01:23.749
on his ledger,

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:24.566
so payday math

00:01:24.566 --> 00:01:26.033
is already done.

00:01:26.505 --> 00:01:27.679
Most teams review a

00:01:27.679 --> 00:01:28.960
small sample of calls

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:29.654
by hand.

00:01:29.654 --> 00:01:30.420
With QA on,

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.382
Conexus scores every recorded

00:01:32.382 --> 00:01:34.040
call over a minute.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.029
Each call is graded

00:01:35.029 --> 00:01:36.321
on your scorecard,

00:01:36.321 --> 00:01:37.216
with reasons and

00:01:37.216 --> 00:01:38.163
a summary.

00:01:38.163 --> 00:01:39.645
A critical flag pauses

00:01:39.645 --> 00:01:41.008
the agent and emails

00:01:41.008 --> 00:01:41.951
your admins.

00:01:41.951 --> 00:01:43.161
An admin unlocks them

00:01:43.161 --> 00:01:44.870
with a one-time code.

00:01:45.283 --> 00:01:46.334
Sales tied to a

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:47.852
call only complete when

00:01:47.852 --> 00:01:49.228
the call passes QA.

00:01:49.228 --> 00:01:50.122
A failing call

00:01:50.122 --> 00:01:51.071
sends the order

00:01:51.071 --> 00:01:52.478
to review instead.

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:53.644
Managers approve,

00:01:53.644 --> 00:01:55.263
reject or re-analyze it

00:01:55.263 --> 00:01:56.909
from one QA queue.

00:01:56.909 --> 00:01:57.726
Bad calls get

00:01:57.726 --> 00:01:58.465
caught early,

00:01:58.465 --> 00:01:59.730
before they turn into

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:01.622
refunds or chargebacks.

00:02:01.983 --> 00:02:03.359
With the dialer add-on,

00:02:03.359 --> 00:02:05.195
supervisors watch every queue

00:02:05.195 --> 00:02:06.291
and agent live.

00:02:06.291 --> 00:02:07.274
Wait times and

00:02:07.274 --> 00:02:08.673
agent statuses update

00:02:08.673 --> 00:02:10.030
as they change.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:10.933
Listen in,

00:02:10.933 --> 00:02:12.085
whisper to the agent,

00:02:12.085 --> 00:02:12.765
or barge into

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:13.618
the call.

00:02:13.618 --> 00:02:14.931
Nobody can listen in

00:02:14.931 --> 00:02:16.414
while a customer enters

00:02:16.414 --> 00:02:17.363
card details.

00:02:17.363 --> 00:02:18.733
Missed calls and every

00:02:18.733 --> 00:02:20.157
agent action are logged

00:02:20.157 --> 00:02:21.661
as they happen.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:22.970
In the dialer,

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:24.123
Loid takes Becky's order

00:02:24.123 --> 00:02:24.958
on the call.

00:02:24.958 --> 00:02:25.572
She reads her

00:02:25.572 --> 00:02:26.349
card out,

00:02:26.349 --> 00:02:27.441
he types it in,

00:02:27.441 --> 00:02:28.115
and it's approved

00:02:28.115 --> 00:02:28.788
while she's still

00:02:28.788 --> 00:02:29.717
on the line.

00:02:29.717 --> 00:02:31.096
No card handy?

00:02:31.096 --> 00:02:32.086
Yor emails Damian

00:02:32.086 --> 00:02:33.263
a payment link,

00:02:33.263 --> 00:02:34.207
and the order waits

00:02:34.207 --> 00:02:35.311
until he pays.

00:02:35.311 --> 00:02:36.807
It works with NMI,

00:02:36.807 --> 00:02:38.060
Authorize.net,

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:39.329
Stripe and Revolv3.

00:02:39.329 --> 00:02:40.522
Conexus keeps a token

00:02:40.522 --> 00:02:41.855
and the last four,

00:02:41.855 --> 00:02:42.520
never the full

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:43.645
card number.

00:02:44.072 --> 00:02:45.292
Where's my order?

00:02:45.292 --> 00:02:46.547
Franky opens Henry's order

00:02:46.547 --> 00:02:47.663
and sees it shipped,

00:02:47.663 --> 00:02:48.664
with tracking.

00:02:48.664 --> 00:02:49.769
The tracking email went

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:50.885
out on its own,

00:02:50.885 --> 00:02:51.711
and it's logged

00:02:51.711 --> 00:02:53.179
on Henry's timeline.

00:02:53.179 --> 00:02:54.633
Sylvia doesn't recognize

00:02:54.633 --> 00:02:55.649
a charge?

00:02:55.649 --> 00:02:56.683
Yor checks the billing

00:02:56.683 --> 00:02:57.842
descriptor of the gateway

00:02:57.842 --> 00:02:58.854
that took it.

00:02:58.854 --> 00:02:59.989
Refunds start from

00:02:59.989 --> 00:03:01.400
the order's transactions,

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.563
and a double click

00:03:02.563 --> 00:03:03.903
never refunds twice.

00:03:03.903 --> 00:03:04.919
The refund email

00:03:04.919 --> 00:03:05.468
goes out,

00:03:05.468 --> 00:03:06.566
and it rolls into

00:03:06.566 --> 00:03:08.700
the Refund Summary report.

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:10.435
When a Shopify shopper

00:03:10.435 --> 00:03:11.570
leaves at checkout,

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:12.484
the cart lands

00:03:12.484 --> 00:03:13.343
in Conexus as

00:03:13.343 --> 00:03:14.628
an abandoned order.

00:03:14.628 --> 00:03:15.949
Carts are checked every

00:03:15.949 --> 00:03:17.270
15 minutes and assigned

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:18.134
to an agent to

00:03:18.134 --> 00:03:19.064
call back.

00:03:19.064 --> 00:03:20.007
Orders also flow

00:03:20.007 --> 00:03:21.376
in from WooCommerce,

00:03:21.376 --> 00:03:22.186
ClickBank,

00:03:22.186 --> 00:03:23.471
SamCart and more.

00:03:23.471 --> 00:03:24.660
Fulfillment goes out to

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.118
ShipStation and others,

00:03:26.118 --> 00:03:27.771
and tracking comes back.

00:03:28.238 --> 00:03:29.588
It's Fern's first day,

00:03:29.588 --> 00:03:30.177
and she can

00:03:30.177 --> 00:03:31.091
just ask Nexa.

00:03:31.091 --> 00:03:32.163
Nexa answers from

00:03:32.163 --> 00:03:33.352
your own docs,

00:03:33.352 --> 00:03:33.899
and looks up

00:03:33.899 --> 00:03:34.560
the orders she's

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.606
allowed to see.

00:03:35.606 --> 00:03:36.546
Upload a Word

00:03:36.546 --> 00:03:37.485
or PDF script,

00:03:37.485 --> 00:03:38.879
and every call fills

00:03:38.879 --> 00:03:40.865
in the customer's details.

00:03:40.865 --> 00:03:42.083
Publish a new version,

00:03:42.083 --> 00:03:42.997
or roll back to

00:03:42.997 --> 00:03:43.809
an old one in

00:03:43.809 --> 00:03:44.967
one click.

00:03:45.317 --> 00:03:46.983
Browser calls are encrypted,

00:03:46.983 --> 00:03:47.955
and saved cards

00:03:47.955 --> 00:03:48.816
are kept only

00:03:48.816 --> 00:03:49.884
as a token.

00:03:49.884 --> 00:03:50.957
Custom roles decide

00:03:50.957 --> 00:03:52.182
who sees what,

00:03:52.182 --> 00:03:53.087
and each company's

00:03:53.087 --> 00:03:54.299
data stays separate.

00:03:54.299 --> 00:03:55.864
Agent activity lands in

00:03:55.864 --> 00:03:57.388
an append-only log.

00:03:57.388 --> 00:03:59.315
PCI self-assessed,

00:03:59.315 --> 00:04:00.546
HIPAA-ready,

00:04:00.546 --> 00:04:01.885
GDPR-aligned.

00:04:01.885 --> 00:04:03.598
SOC 2 and ISO

00:04:03.598 --> 00:04:06.767
27001 are in progress.

00:04:07.117 --> 00:04:08.308
Coming soon: AI that

00:04:08.308 --> 00:04:09.390
can take and make

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.106
calls alongside your team.

00:04:11.106 --> 00:04:11.901
GIFs are coming

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:12.913
to team chat,

00:04:12.913 --> 00:04:14.097
for every big sale.

00:04:14.097 --> 00:04:15.723
Secure keypad payments are

00:04:15.723 --> 00:04:17.012
on the way: customers

00:04:17.012 --> 00:04:18.133
key in their card,

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:19.002
and the agent

00:04:19.002 --> 00:04:20.193
hears silence.

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:22.010
Texting your customers by

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:23.545
SMS is coming next.

00:04:23.545 --> 00:04:24.840
And we're building Conexus

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.029
Sheets and Docs,

00:04:26.029 --> 00:04:26.943
for your whole team

00:04:26.943 --> 00:04:28.155
to edit together.

00:04:28.155 --> 00:04:29.065
And there's plenty more

00:04:29.065 --> 00:04:30.120
on the way.

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:32.438
Your whole call team,

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:33.412
on one screen.

00:04:33.412 --> 00:04:34.622
Meet Conexus,

00:04:34.622 --> 00:04:35.530
the CRM built

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:36.737
for call teams.

00:04:36.737 --> 00:04:37.693
Book a demo

00:04:37.693 --> 00:04:39.568
at tryconexus.com

